WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:08.508
This is a very densely written
show every detail is so

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:12.054
important, from the design of
the room, to the color palette,

00:00:12.054 --> 00:00:15.891
to the hair, to the costume,
the emotionality of what our

00:00:15.891 --> 00:00:17.184
characters are going through.

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:19.353
Hey look that's, my
sister right there.

00:00:19.645 --> 00:00:22.522
I thought it was a very
complex season for Bradley 

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:26.777
her character didn't just touch
on being queer it touched on

00:00:26.777 --> 00:00:31.198
family with addiction and how we
all get sucked into that vortex

00:00:31.198 --> 00:00:34.451
of an addict's life and
ultimately falling apart

00:00:34.451 --> 00:00:35.994
because you have no
power over that.

00:00:36.662 --> 00:00:37.579
We're past it now!

00:00:37.579 --> 00:00:40.082
Are we? Oh my God that's good
to know I didn't know that we --

00:00:40.082 --> 00:00:42.960
Alex don't do this to us! 
We're finally in a good place.

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:44.753
One thing that Jen
and I discussed

00:00:44.753 --> 00:00:47.089
we wanted to make
sure Chip and Alex

00:00:47.089 --> 00:00:50.133
didn't come across that they
were just like siblings

00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:51.260
yelling at each other.

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:53.136
We wanted to layer everything

00:00:53.136 --> 00:00:55.764
with a deep sense of
dedication and love

00:00:55.764 --> 00:00:57.432
and I think honestly
it's been easy cause

00:00:57.432 --> 00:01:01.478
I just find Jen to be so 
bouyant and she's so alive.

00:01:02.688 --> 00:01:03.730
You're okay.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:05.983
I love the relationship
between Chip and Alex.

00:01:05.983 --> 00:01:08.277
Chip is kind of in love with her
and they each see the

00:01:08.277 --> 00:01:09.820
relationship a little
differently.

00:01:10.112 --> 00:01:11.697
I think Alex she's getting out

00:01:11.697 --> 00:01:15.075
beyond her narcissism enough to
understand, she's taken

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:18.912
Chip for granted and he has
always been there for her.

00:01:20.122 --> 00:01:23.250
Mitch was... Mitch is a human
being.

00:01:24.293 --> 00:01:26.503
Karen was so beautiful
in that scene

00:01:27.129 --> 00:01:29.548
and it spoke beautifully
to the moment too that

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:32.009
you are some of the
things that have

00:01:32.009 --> 00:01:33.427
happened to you
in your life.

00:01:33.427 --> 00:01:35.304
You're not just the
one terrible thing.

00:01:35.512 --> 00:01:37.264
He really does have
young children.

00:01:37.681 --> 00:01:38.598
It's complex!

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:41.685
We're getting to see in
their eyes, in their faces.

00:01:41.852 --> 00:01:44.229
All of the feelings that
they had about Mitch.

00:01:44.646 --> 00:01:46.023
And now they have
to reconcile them

00:01:46.023 --> 00:01:47.190
because he's
no longer there.

00:01:47.441 --> 00:01:50.527
We really see Mia
spilling out all of the

00:01:50.527 --> 00:01:53.113
feelings that she has
in the midst of this grief.

00:01:53.322 --> 00:01:55.032
I think I knew the real him

00:01:55.032 --> 00:01:56.867
and the book doesn't
get the real him.

00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:59.202
The real him is dead!

00:02:00.162 --> 00:02:02.789
An actor is only successful as
the director she

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:05.792
is able to collaborate with and
Victoria Mahoney,

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:08.837
who directs episode 208 is
an extraordinary collaborator.

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:11.048
That first day I
worked with her,

00:02:11.506 --> 00:02:14.343
I just felt I'm
madly in love!

00:02:14.343 --> 00:02:16.428
It's like, where have you
been all of our lives?

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:19.598
Knows how to speak
to actors so beautifully.

00:02:19.848 --> 00:02:20.807
She was incredible.

00:02:21.266 --> 00:02:21.725
GO!

00:02:21.725 --> 00:02:24.561
Filming this episode
was such a whirlwind

00:02:24.561 --> 00:02:27.147
in an already
intense environment.

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:29.149
Thankfully my character is
always in sneakers,

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:32.903
but I literally had to run.
We were sweating doing that.

00:02:33.403 --> 00:02:35.489
We're interrupting with
some breaking news.

00:02:35.697 --> 00:02:38.325
Our stories are told through our
characters' points of view.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:42.162
They're complicated as is life
as is human emotion.

00:02:42.454 --> 00:02:44.414
One moment you're happy,
one moment you're

00:02:44.414 --> 00:02:46.666
trying to figure out
where do I fit?

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.210
How do I get there?
What do I do?

